    {
      "p": "因为…，所以… — because …, so …",
      "e": "Chinese usually keeps BOTH halves of the pair, while English drops one of them. 因为 opens the reason, 所以 opens the result.",
      "x": "因为下雨了，所以我们没出去。 — Because it rained, we didn't go out."
    },
    {
      "p": "verb + 一次 — counting times",
      "e": "次 counts how many times an action happens, and it goes after the verb: 洗一次 (wash one load), 去过两次 (been there twice).",
      "x": "这件衣服我洗了两次。 — I washed this shirt twice."
    },
